      "content": "It's more accurate to say the current mainstream scientific view emphasizes complexity rather than dismissing any single perspective outright. The most robust scientific position acknowledges both biological foundations and the significant role of social and psychological factors in shaping gender. Therefore, viewing the biological perspective as entirely \"incorrect\" overlooks its established role in human biology. Rather than one side being \"right\" and the other \"wrong,\" scientific understanding continues to evolve by integrating evidence from multiple fields.",
      "source": "target",
